==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Earth King Sodom''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''God-Emperor Sodom''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Sodom is an incredibly slow unit, making him good for stalling in stages when feasible, but his high cost doesn't make him any better otherwise. His knockback ability also improves his matchup against Floating enemies due to their low range, but his non-guaranteed activation and attack rate often gets in the way.

What makes things even worse is the very niche he occupies. Many Floating enemies, as mentioned before, are short-ranged pushers, and his range of 390 only allows him to serve as a secondary line of defense, and while his knockback immunity helps to prevent him from being pushed around by the likes of [[Trolly Blogger]], it hurts his survivability greatly due to having only 2 knockbacks, while lacking other more useful immunities a tank should have. Admittedly, he does have good matchups against [[Shy Boy]]s and Teacher Bun Bun variants, with acceptable performance, but that's all he offers. Floating enemies often are backed by foes of other traits, dramatically reducing his utility, and late-game pushers often boast monstrous stats to the point where tanks like him simply become unusable. If crowd-control and damage are needed, [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman]] and [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo]] will help in taking them out and don't have many of his issues. At best, he may help in stopping [[Brollow]] swarms from advancing.

==='''True Form'''===
Sodom gains increased range, health, damage and knockback chance in his True Form. Unfortunately, he still has the same problem as his previous forms, wherein his attacks are too slow, and his range is still only mediocre.

==='''Talents'''===
Sodom is not a good uber to invest in, but still has a few points of interest.

Through '''Target Relic''' and '''Curse Immunity''', Sodom gains another niche against Relic enemies, but he doesn't stand out particularly due to his slow attack rate, which prevents him from consistently displacing or eliminating them. '''Weaken''' does help him last a little longer, but there are many better options, and even at max level, it only has a pathetic 12% uptime with its 30% chance and 4.8 second duration. The basic stat boosts are only worth considering with the help of [[Catseye]]s.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
'''Sage Slayer''' is an interesting Talent, as it allows Sodom to counter [[Adherence to Virtue]], giving him '''2.5 million''' health against Soractes and allowing his crowd-control abilities to bypass Soractes' Sage Resistance. However, Sodom is still very vulnerable to the Doge Darks on that stage, and there are better options for that stage that don't cost 15 Dark Catseyes for a rather niche unit.

'''Behemoth Slayer''' also sees little use. It does allow Sodom to counter [[Pterowl Hazuku]]/[[Ensanglion the Calamity]] more effectively (he stands outside of Hazuku's blindspot, and does have the bulk to tank both), no other Floating Behemoths exist. He fares better
against Relic Behemoths like [[Ultima Beast Naala]], [[Iguanidae Ibilujon]], [[Ancient Magamojoe]] and [[Great Ape Luza]] (which [[Birth of True Man|does appear with Hazuku once]]), but again these matchups are generally unfavorable if other threats get in the way, not to mention Ibilujon and Magamojoe are Immune to Knockback.

'''Weaken Immunity''' is not very useful for its high NP cost, especially when considering how rare the Weaken effect is and how Sodom is rarely used for his damage.

